## Context

Premier enfant de [[0834]]. Le MVP ne donne aucun accès aux documents bruts :
les cartes source affichent une URL d'origine et une empreinte tronquée. Le
registre `data/jetp/manifest.csv` (307 sources, 262 collectées, 84 PDF et
154 HTML archivés) et le snapshot DVC `data/jetp/documents/` existent déjà.
Ce ticket les rend lisibles, et livre au passage le composant de tableau
filtrable que [[0836]], [[0838]] et [[0839]] réutilisent.

Les documents s'ouvrent en local seulement. `deliverables/jetp-observatory/README.md`
exclut leur redistribution publique ; l'édition publique ne sert que le
registre et l'URL d'origine.

## Relevant files

- `data/jetp/manifest.csv` — registre des sources : id, pays, date de collecte, statut, type, empreinte, chemin de stockage, URL finale
- `data/jetp/documents/` — objets archivés par empreinte (DVC, `make jetp-data` après `dvc pull`)
- `deliverables/jetp-observatory/app.js`, `index.html`, `styles.css` — site statique
- `scripts/jetp/build_observatory.py`, `scripts/jetp/_observatory_data.py` — génération des JSON de vue
- `scripts/jetp/build_observatory_bundle.py` — édition publique, doit exclure les documents
- `scripts/analysis/jetp_observatory.mk` — cibles `jetp-observatory` et `jetp-observatory-preview`
- `tests/browser/jetp_observatory.py` — recette navigateur Playwright
- `docs/jetp-storage.md` — règles de provisionnement des snapshots

## Dependencies

Aucun ticket amont : premier de la vague 1 issue de [[0834]], sans bloqueur.
En aval, [[0836]], [[0838]] et [[0839]] réutilisent la vue `data/documents.json`
et le composant `filterTable` livrés ici ; ils sont bloqués par ce ticket,
jamais l'inverse.

## Actions

1. **Vue `data/documents.json`** (une entrée par ligne de
   `data/jetp/manifest.csv`, aucune jointure avec `sources.csv` — le registre
   porte déjà tous les champs demandés : `country`, `retrieved_at`, `status`,
   `content_type`, `sha256`, `size_bytes`, `storage_path`, `final_url`).
   - Ajouter `document_entry(row, available)` dans `scripts/jetp/_observatory_data.py`,
     à côté de `public_event`/`historical_record`/`timeline` : transformation
     pure (aucun accès disque), qui construit une entrée depuis une ligne du
     registre. Champs de sortie : `id` (`source_id`), `country`,
     `collected_on` (`retrieved_at` ou `None`), `status` (valeur brute,
     jamais reformulée), `content_type` (ou `None`), `size_bytes` (entier ou
     `None`), `sha256` (ou `None`), `url` (`final_url` ou `None`), `error`
     (ou `None`), `local_path` — `f"documents/{storage_path}"` seulement si
     `storage_path` est non vide **et** figure dans `available` ; sinon `None`.
   - Ajouter `documents_data(root, tables)` dans `scripts/jetp/build_observatory.py`,
     à côté de `comparison_data` : construit `available` en vérifiant, pour
     chaque `storage_path` non vide de `tables['manifest']`, si
     `(root / 'data/jetp/documents' / storage_path).is_file()` ; trie les
     lignes par `source_id` (sortie déterministe) ; retourne
     `{'documents': [document_entry(row, available) for row in rows]}`.
     `tables['manifest']` est déjà chargé par `read_inputs` (`'manifest'` est
     déjà dans `TABLES`) — ne pas relire le CSV.
   - Étendre les choix `--view` de `main()` avec `'documents'` et la branche
     `elif args.view == 'documents': result = documents_data(ROOT, tables)`.
   - Ajouter `'documents'` à `JETP_OBSERVATORY_VIEWS` dans
     `scripts/analysis/jetp_observatory.mk` : la règle générique
     `$(JETP_OBSERVATORY)/data/%.json` produit alors `documents.json` sans
     changement supplémentaire (`manifest.csv` et `documents.dvc` sont déjà
     dans `JETP_OBSERVATORY_INPUTS`).

2. **Composant de tableau filtrable**, dans `app.js`, signature figée pour
   0836/0838/0839 :

   ```js
   // filterTable(id, rows, opts) -> { head, mount }
   //   id          unique DOM id prefix, e.g. "documents"
   //   rows        full unfiltered row array (caller already scoped the data)
   //   opts.facets [{ key, label, options }]  one <select> per facet;
   //               `options` is the caller-supplied, already-deduped/sorted
   //               value list (reuse the existing `options()` helper);
   //               a row matches when row[facet.key] === selected value.
   //   opts.search { placeholder, text(row) }  `text(row)` returns the
   //               lower-cased haystack string for the free-text field
   //               (mirrors cataloguePage's `[p.name, p.operator, ...]`).
   //   opts.columns [{ label, cell(row) }]     one <th>/<td> pair each;
   //               `cell` returns an already-`esc()`-escaped HTML string.
   //   opts.empty  message for the `.empty` fallback (no rows match)
   //   opts.resultNoun  plural noun for the count line, e.g. "sources"
   //   opts.pageSize    rows per page (new capability; neither existing
   //               page paginates today)
   // head: HTML string (filters block + `#${id}-count` aria-live paragraph +
   //   `#${id}-results` div) to splice into main.innerHTML.
   // mount(): call once head is in the DOM; wires listeners on
   //   `#${id}-search` / `#${id}-filter-<key>` / pager controls, resets to
   //   page 1 on every filter change, and renders the first pass.
   ```

   Reuse this shape for the new Documents page. Retrofit `cataloguePage` and
   `comparisonPage` onto `filterTable` only if the resulting diff stays small
   (per Imagine); otherwise leave them and open a follow-up ticket — do not
   let that retrofit block this ticket's exit criteria. No new CSS classes
   required beyond pager controls reusing `.button light`; no dependency
   (`package.json` stays absent).

3. **Page « Documents »**: add `documentsPage()` (dispatched from `render()`
   via `else if (page === "documents") documentsPage();`, inserted before the
   `methodsPage()` fallback) built on `filterTable("documents", documentsData.documents, …)`
   with facets on `country`, `status`, `content_type` and free-text search on
   `id`/`url`. Columns: source id, country, status (pill), content type, size,
   an « copie archivée » cell (see action 5 — link only when `local_path` is
   non-null, otherwise plain disabled-looking text), an « origine » cell
   (always present, `<a target="_blank" rel="noopener">` on `url`, reusing
   `cleanURL()`/`esc()`). Insert `<a href="#documents">Documents</a>` into
   `index.html`'s `<nav>` right after `<a href="#countries">Countries</a>` and
   before `<a href="#projects">Projects</a>`. In `start()`, add
   `load("documents")` to the `Promise.all` alongside the existing views and
   assign it to a new module-level `documentsData` (not `documents`, to avoid
   reading like the DOM `document` global), declared alongside the existing
   `let overview, countries, comparison, editions, evidence, m1a, projects;`.

4. **Local-preview document folder** (`deliverables/jetp-observatory/documents/`):
   - Add a `jetp-observatory-documents` target in `scripts/analysis/jetp_observatory.mk`,
     prerequisite of `jetp-observatory-preview` only (not of `jetp-observatory`,
     so the JSON build and the public bundle never depend on whether a local
     snapshot happens to exist). Reuse the reflink idiom already in
     `.githooks/post-checkout`'s `initialize_jetp_snapshots()`: stage with
     `cp -RL --reflink=always` into a `mktemp -d` sibling, then `mv -Tn` into
     place; fall back to `ln -s` (symlink) when reflink is unsupported; warn
     and exit 0 (never fail the build) when `data/jetp/documents/` itself is
     absent (offline/no-DVC machine).
   - Add `deliverables/jetp-observatory/documents/` to `.gitignore` as a
     directory entry — the existing `deliverables/*/*.pdf` / `*.docx` globs
     are one level too shallow for `documents/objects/<prefix>/<sha>.<ext>`.
   - Fix the real bundle-exclusion risk this folder creates: `_capture()` in
     `scripts/jetp/_observatory_bundle.py` walks `site.rglob('*')` over the
     **whole** `SITE` tree with no exclusion, so once this folder exists on a
     machine, every `freeze_bundle`/`build_candidate` call — including the
     existing `test_interrupted_candidate_preserves_accepted_and_restores_offline`
     in `tests/test_jetp_observatory_bundle.py`, which runs `freeze_bundle`
     against this real repo — would start embedding archived document bytes
     into the bundle. Add `SITE_EXCLUDE = ('documents',)` and a
     `site_files(site)` generator to `scripts/jetp/_bundle_inventory.py` that
     yields files under `site` skipping any path under an excluded top-level
     name; change `_capture()` to call `site_files(site)` instead of
     `site.rglob('*')` directly.
   - Add `'documents'` to `VIEWS` in `_bundle_inventory.py` so `documents.json`
     (registry + origin URL, never the archived bytes) stays in the public
     edition, per the README's stated boundary. `routes()` currently iterates
     `VIEWS[2:]` assuming those entries are country codes with a `projects`
     key — introduce `COUNTRIES = ('ZAF', 'IDN', 'VNM', 'SEN')` and make
     `routes()` iterate `COUNTRIES` directly, so `'documents'` can join `VIEWS`
     without breaking that assumption.
   - Out of scope, write down instead of fixing: `scripts/jetp/_public_release.py`
     (whole-tree copy at a pinned commit) does not go through this exclusion
     path at all. Add one sentence to `deliverables/jetp-observatory/README.md`
     (near "What is included") stating that `documents/` is local-preview only,
     excluded from the bundle and from any public release — nothing more; do
     not modify `_public_release.py` in this ticket.

5. **`#page=N` fragment**: this is native PDF-viewer behaviour (Chromium/Firefox
   both honour `file.pdf#page=N`); nothing server-side to implement. Add a
   small `documentHref(entry, page)` helper in `app.js` —
   `entry.local_path ? entry.local_path + (page ? '#page=' + page : '') : null`
   — and use it for the Documents table's « copie archivée » cell, so 0836 can
   call the same helper with a computed page number instead of re-deriving
   link construction. No JSON field encodes a printed-page-to-PDF-page offset
   in this ticket (per Imagine, only 279 VNM rows carry a `PDF pages N`
   locator, and computing that mapping is 0836's job) — verify the fragment
   manually per the Verification checklist.

6. **Lexical replacement**: grep confirms exactly one reader-facing instance
   in a file this ticket touches — `m1aSection()` in `app.js`: "These four
   tables preserve every row of six selected source layers before canonical
   matching." → "…six selected extraction sub-layers…" (the site is
   English-language throughout; "sous-couche d'extraction" names the concept,
   not a literal string to insert). `build_m1a_inventories.py`'s docstring
   ("one bounded source layer") is an internal comment, not MVP reader text —
   leave it out of scope for this ticket.

## Test

Red : `tests/test_jetp_observatory_documents.py`, fast tier (pure Python +
`tmp_path`, no subprocess, no marker needed).

Fixture — four `manifest.csv`-shaped rows and a `tmp_path/'data/jetp/documents'`
directory containing **only** the PDF's bytes at its `storage_path`:

- `vnm-collected-pdf`: `status='collected'`, `content_type='application/pdf'`,
  `storage_path='objects/aa/pdf.pdf'`, `sha256='a'*64`, `size_bytes='120000'`,
  `final_url='https://example.test/rmp.pdf'`.
- `zaf-collected-html`: `status='collected'`, `content_type='text/html'`,
  `storage_path='objects/bb/reg.html'` — **not** written to the fixture
  snapshot directory, despite `status='collected'`.
- `sen-blocked`: `status='blocked'`, `storage_path=''`, `error='HTTP 403'`.
- `idn-fetch-error`: `status='fetch_error'`, `storage_path=''`,
  `error='RetryError: ...'`.

Call `documents_data(tmp_path, {'manifest': rows})` and assert:

- `{d['id'] for d in result['documents']} == {'vnm-collected-pdf', 'zaf-collected-html', 'sen-blocked', 'idn-fetch-error'}`
  — exactly these four, nothing merged (e.g. by shared `sha256`) or invented.
- PDF entry: `local_path == 'documents/objects/aa/pdf.pdf'` (the registry's own
  path, never reconstructed from `sha256`/`content_type`), and `country`,
  `sha256`, `size_bytes == 120000`, `content_type` equal the source row
  verbatim.
- HTML entry: `status == 'collected'` **and** `local_path is None` — this is
  the assertion that distinguishes "preserved" from "invented/different": an
  implementation that derives availability from `status` alone (instead of
  checking the snapshot directory) would wrongly set `local_path` here and
  must fail until the disk check exists. This is the antipattern check: a
  first-draft test asserting only `len(result['documents']) == 4` would be a
  tautology that a "merge the two failures into one row" or "invent a filler
  row" implementation could also satisfy; comparing the exact id set plus this
  same-status-different-outcome pair closes that gap.
- `sen-blocked` and `idn-fetch-error`: `local_path is None`, `status` and
  `error` preserved verbatim, `url` (from `final_url`) preserved — neither is
  dropped or folded into a generic "unavailable" status.
- Determinism: `[d['id'] for d in result['documents']] == sorted(row['source_id'] for row in rows)`.

Playwright (`tests/browser/jetp_observatory.py`) additions, appended after the
existing checks, against the real running preview (307 manifest rows):

- `page.goto(url + '/#documents')`; wait for the filters selector; assert the
  count line shows `307` before any filter is applied.
- Select country=SEN and status=blocked; assert
  `page.locator('#documents-results tbody tr').count() == 5` (exact count on
  the real registry: `country=='SEN' and status=='blocked'`).
- Click the « copie archivée » link for `zaf-jet-investment-register-q1-2026`
  and assert the response/download is the archived HTML snapshot — covers the
  0834 recipe line "le snapshot HTML du registre JET ZAF s'ouvre depuis la
  page Documents".
- Do not encode the VNM page-139→155 mapping in Playwright — no such data
  exists in this ticket's scope; keep it as the existing manual Verification
  checklist item.

## Verification

- [ ] `make jetp-observatory-preview` sert la page Documents et le PDF du RMP VNM s'ouvre à la page 139 via `documents/<empreinte>.pdf#page=155`
- [ ] Le snapshot HTML du registre JET ZAF s'ouvre depuis la page Documents
- [ ] Filtrer sur pays = SEN et statut = bloqué donne les lignes attendues du registre
- [ ] Le bundle public ne contient aucun objet archivé
- [ ] `tests/browser/jetp_observatory.py` exerce un filtre et une ouverture de document

## Invariants

- Le registre reste la seule source de vérité ; la vue n'ajoute aucune ligne.
- Un document absent du snapshot reste listé avec son statut, jamais retiré.
- Les autres vues du MVP et les tables M1a restent identiques octet pour octet.
- `make check-fast` et `make lint` passent.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] La page Documents liste les 307 sources avec filtres et recherche
- [ ] Chaque source collectée et présente dans le snapshot s'ouvre en local
- [ ] Le composant de tableau est exporté et documenté pour les tickets suivants
- [ ] Le bundle public exclut les documents et le README le dit
- [ ] Recette 0834 : ouverture du RMP VNM page 139 et du registre ZAF réussie

## Out of scope

Extraction de contenu, liens entre lignes et documents (0836), déploiement
public (0727).

## Imagine (raid 2026-09-17)

Verdict : exécuter, avec simplification. `app.js` code déjà deux fois le
motif filtre + tableau (`cataloguePage`, `comparisonPage`) : entrées de
filtre, prédicat, compteur `aria-live`, repli `.empty`, sans fonction
commune. Le composant de l'action 2 est l'extraction de cette forme, pas une
conception nouvelle ; les deux pages existantes ne sont reprises que si le
diff reste petit, sinon ticket de suite. Aucune bibliothèque : pas de
`package.json`, le README interdit les dépendances JavaScript. API initiale
étroite (facettes, recherche, pagination, compte). L'exclusion du bundle
(action 4) vit dans `scripts/jetp/_bundle_inventory.py` (`VIEWS`, `SITE`,
pointeur `documents.dvc`). Angle mort : le pipeline d'édition citable
(`scripts/jetp/_public_release.py`, copie de l'arbre entier à un commit
épinglé) ne passe pas par cette exclusion ; le choix « registre + URL
d'origine seulement » doit être écrit pour lui aussi, ou déclaré hors
périmètre jusqu'à la prochaine édition. Descente à la page : seules les 279
lignes VNM portent un localisateur `PDF pages N` ; l'ouverture à la page est
SA (HTML) et VN (PDF) par construction, pas un trait à quatre pays.
